CAT = "rdPractice"; SEG = "PRA"
Q = [
("A supplement company offers an RDN a paid trip if she recommends its product to clients. What does the Code of Ethics require?",
 "Avoid or disclose the conflict", ["Accept if the product is safe", "Accept and tell no one", "Report the company to the FDA"],
 "The Code of Ethics for the Nutrition and Dietetics Profession asks practitioners to avoid conflicts of interest and to disclose any that exist. Recommendations must rest on evidence and the client's interest."),
("An outpatient clinic gives its limited counseling slots by nutrition risk, not by insurance or ability to pay. Which ethical principle does this reflect?",
 "Justice", ["Autonomy", "Beneficence", "Fidelity"],
 "Justice is the fair distribution of care and resources. Autonomy is a person's right to make informed choices, beneficence is acting for the person's good, and fidelity is keeping promises and trust."),
("A new graduate is asked to manage insulin drips. Which document helps her judge whether this is within her practice?",
 "Scope and Standards of Practice", ["Hospital mission statement", "Dietary Guidelines for Americans", "Facility diet manual"],
 "The Scope of Practice and the Standards of Practice and Professional Performance, with state law and facility privileges, define what a practitioner may do and at what level of competence."),
("An RDN looks up the chart of a neighbor she is not treating, out of curiosity. What rule does this break?",
 "HIPAA privacy rule", ["FERPA student rule", "Stark self-referral law", "OSHA record rule"],
 "Under HIPAA a workforce member may use protected health information only as needed for treatment, payment or operations. Viewing a record without a work reason is a privacy violation even if nothing is shared."),
("When releasing records for billing, an RDN sends only the parts the payer needs. Which HIPAA standard is this?",
 "Minimum necessary", ["Right of access", "Breach notification", "Notice of privacy practices"],
 "The minimum necessary standard limits uses and disclosures of PHI to what the purpose requires. It does not apply to disclosures to a provider for treatment."),
("An electronic health record alert warns that a renal patient was ordered a high-potassium supplement. What is this feature?",
 "Clinical decision support", ["Interoperability standard", "Telehealth platform", "Data warehouse"],
 "Clinical decision support gives the clinician patient-specific prompts and alerts at the point of care. Interoperability is the ability of systems to exchange data with each other."),
("In the marketing mix, a new grab-and-go salad kiosk near the hospital lobby is a decision about which P?",
 "Place", ["Product", "Price", "Promotion"],
 "Place is where and how customers get the product. The salad itself is the product, its cost to the customer is price, and the signs and coupons about it are promotion."),
("A SWOT analysis notes that a competing café is opening next door. Where does this go?",
 "Threats", ["Weaknesses", "Opportunities", "Strengths"],
 "Strengths and weaknesses are internal; opportunities and threats are external. A new competitor is an outside force that could hurt sales, so it is a threat."),
("A hospital café redesigns its menu for night-shift staff only. What marketing step is this?",
 "Targeting a market segment", ["Mass marketing to all customers", "Setting a cost-plus price", "Writing a press release"],
 "Segmentation splits customers into groups with shared needs, and targeting picks one to serve with a fitted offer. Mass marketing offers one product to everyone."),
("A local TV station asks an RDN about a viral diet trend. What should guide the answer?",
 "Current scientific evidence", ["The station's sponsors", "Personal food preferences", "The trend's popularity"],
 "The Code of Ethics asks practitioners to present information based on current evidence and to distinguish fact from opinion. Public relations work builds trust only when it is accurate."),
("An RDN learns a colleague is billing for sessions that never happened. What does the Code of Ethics expect?",
 "Report it to the right authority", ["Ignore it unless someone asks", "Call the patients to confirm", "Post about it on social media"],
 "The Code asks practitioners to report illegal or unethical conduct to the employer, CDR or other appropriate authority. Discussing it publicly could breach privacy and due process."),
("Which term means providing nutrition care by secure video to a client at home?",
 "Telehealth", ["Informatics", "Interoperability", "Health literacy"],
 "Telehealth delivers care at a distance using technology such as secure video. State licensure rules for the client's location still apply, and they vary by state."),
]
